{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'B0|normaliz|golden|print-stable|corrupt|live-set|client harness|JVM to Dart|remote stream|pairing-mismatch|shadowed-free|absent|DHT peer' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '225,260p;590,630p;1975,2010p;2220,2285p'; git show df7cf1f4 --stat 2>/dev/null; git show 00da7c5d -- docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 2>/dev/null | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"129:  content over remote streams (`dao.stream.remote.md` section 8);\n159:in a file, behind a socket, or on a DHT peer changes how bytes are\n360:                 absent entry                       -> :absent\n362:                 absent payload                     -> :absent\n375:                 name bound in free env or store    -> :shadowed-free\n401:   yet is `:absent` now, which is the honest answer at this moment; a\n433:   ascending, bounded, exact live-set rules. Every validator includes\n541:     free env or store is `:shadowed-free`; anything else is\n568:| `:absent`               | 1 or 2 | no index entry, or no payload at the     |\n586:| `:shadowed-free`        | 5b     | an obligation's name is bound by the     |\n610:| `:pairing-mismatch`     | verify | B6's same-root check (now a case of      |\n747:live-set rules; free names are `[:load-free rd name]` operands across all\n762:`:pairing-mismatch` reason is retained as the name of a\n796:| remote content        | ring buffer  | remote streams  | content's     |\n807:ring buffers or reflections of remote streams, with the shared ingress\n906:{:yin.link/id [:t0 7] :status :refused :reason :absent :address a}\n971:`(:modules state)` alone: present, the module name; absent, a thrown\n1018:   7.3) is neither linked nor absent: the requiring task joins that\n1246:     table only grows, and an absent row is a host assembly defect --\n1445:    a key the module store lacks is absent, exactly as a top-level\n1446:    read of an absent key is; engine resources are unreachable\n1689:    implement that exact profile, or the tree is `:absent`, or the tree\n1769:  An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\n1852:  counted. Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is `:absent`. More than\n1902:entered as an already-linked manifest with `:yin.module/tree` absent,\n1983:two new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n1984:that row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n2032:store is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n2075:the same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\n   225\t  `segment-key` of its canonical instruction vector, and\n   226\t  `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section 4.1 defines a tree's address as its\n   227\t  root row's id, itself a `segment-key`. Here the identity's preimage is\n   228\t  the payload, so the identity is a storage address, carries a hash\n   229\t  algorithm of its own, and changes when the storage encoder changes.\n   230\t  **Strict decoupling therefore holds only for H and R today.** UCF\n   231\t  accepts this (\"UCF must not mint a second addressing scheme\"); this\n   232\t  document inherits it, verifies these identities under the algorithm\n   233\t  they carry (section 4.1), and records the amendment that would pin\n   234\t  them as a UCF and code-as-tuples decision, not a linker one (section\n   235\t  12).\n   236\t\n   237\t**Module name.** A symbol resolved through a name environment to a\n   238\tmanifest address (section 8). A name is a claim of whoever asserted it;\n   239\tthe manifest it resolves to is content and is verified like any other,\n   240\tincluding that it declares the name it was resolved under.\n   241\t\n   242\tThe relation among them, for one module and one backend:\n   243\t\n   244\t```text\n   245\tname 'my.lib\n   246\t  --(name environment, one accepted assertion)--> manifest address\n   247\t  --(fetch, verify, name check)-->                manifest value\n   248\t  --(:yin.module/tree)-->                         canonical tree address\n   249\t  --(:yin.module/derivations, format f)-->        derivation record\n   250\t  --(record :yin.ledger/output)-->                format identity\n   251\t  --(format index)-->                             storage address\n   252\t  --(fetch, verify)-->                            image value\n   253\t```\n   254\t\n   255\tTwo indexes appear: the name environment (name to manifest address) and\n   256\tthe format index (identity to storage address). Both are linker-local\n   257\tstate (section 6.2); neither ever travels on the link stream.\n   258\t\n   259\t## 4. The fetch pipeline\n   260\t\n   590\t| `:module-name-mismatch` | 8.1    | the manifest declares a name other than  |\n   591\t|                         |        | the one it was resolved under            |\n   592\t| `:ambiguous-name`       | 8.2    | more than one accepted assertion for a   |\n   593\t|                         |        | name at the snapshot                     |\n   594\t| `:derivation-mismatch`  | 8.1    | an image's derivation record does not    |\n   595\t|                         |        | lead from the manifest's tree, or a      |\n   596\t|                         |        | verifying re-lowering disagrees          |\n   597\t| `:unverified-derivation`| 8.1    | a verifying link cannot recompute the    |\n   598\t|                         |        | derivation (profile not implemented, or  |\n   599\t|                         |        | tree unavailable) and refuses to trust   |\n   600\t| `:unauthenticated`      | 8.2    | an assertion carries no proof the        |\n   601\t|                         |        | composition's verifier accepts           |\n   602\t| `:export-missing`       | 7.3    | the evaluated module did not bind an     |\n   603\t|                         |        | export the manifest names                |\n   604\t| `:require-cycle`        | 7.4    | a child install requires a module that   |\n   605\t|                         |        | is itself installing in its ancestry     |\n   606\t| `:foreign-image`        | 7.3    | an exported closure originates in an     |\n   607\t|                         |        | image this scheduler never verified      |\n   608\t| `:binding-mismatch`     | 7.3    | a positional closure marker lowered into |\n   609\t|                         |        | a named kernel, or the reverse           |\n   610\t| `:pairing-mismatch`     | verify | B6's same-root check (now a case of      |\n   611\t|                         |        | `:derivation-mismatch`, kept by name)    |\n   612\t\n   613\t`:unsupported-format` is the linker's instance of the host-boundary rule\n   614\tthat a host with no implementation for an effect emits a qualified\n   615\tunsupported result, \"a correct outcome, not a gap to be filled\"\n   616\t(`datom.world.md`). It lets a receiver decline an R request and, where\n   617\tthe composition permits, fall back to H by the manifest's derivations.\n   618\t\n   619\tA stepped link additionally reports `:pending` (section 6.3), which is\n   620\tnot a refusal: it is the \"not yet\" of a non-blocking read.\n   621\t\n   622\t## 5. Format records for the four backends\n   623\t\n   624\tThree records bind existing code; the AST record's free-name scanner is\n   625\tthe section 4.5 query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`, implemented as\n   626\t`yin.vm/free-names`.\n   627\t\n   628\t### 5.1 `:yin.ast/code` (the AST walker)\n   629\t\n   630\t```clojure\n  1975\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1976\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1977\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1978\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1979\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1980\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1981\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1982\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1983\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1984\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1985\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1986\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1987\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1988\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1989\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1990\t`:blake3`.\n  1991\t\n  1992\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1993\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.content.step` on a\n  1994\trequest and response pair, local ring buffers or reflections\n  1995\t(`dao.stream.remote.md` section 8), served by\n  1996\t`dao.jing.content/serve-step`, with the shared ingress check\n  1997\t`dao.jing/accept-bytes!`. Reimplement\n  1998\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1999\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  2000\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  2001\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  2002\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  2003\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  2004\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  2005\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  2006\tthe server driven by the test.\n  2007\t\n  2008\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  2009\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  2010\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  2220\t    issue three requests on one link pair with three distinct ids, and\n  2221\t    each restores on its own.\n  2222\t17. On every backend, an exported closure applied in the parent after\n  2223\t    `linked` runs the same body it ran in the child; a stack and a\n  2224\t    register closure exported from a child whose image was appended at\n  2225\t    a nonzero offset in the parent resolve to the relocated pc; a\n  2226\t    walker closure lowers to a body structurally equal to the child's;\n  2227\t    on every backend, a parent parked mid-program at a nonzero pc with\n  2228\t    a non-empty stack, frames, and continuation resumes after\n  2229\t    `attach-image` at the same pc with the same stack, frames, and\n  2230\t    restore identities, and every register the loader would have reset\n  2231\t    is unchanged; the parked entry predates the attach, its recorded\n  2232\t    image is a row of the offset table, no restore writes `:segment`\n  2233\t    from an entry, and `:hash` is never a restore key; on the\n  2234\t    register backend, an image attached by a nested require while a\n  2235\t    call is in flight survives the callee's return: no frame carries\n  2236\t    or restores `:segment` or `:hash`, and the caller resumes in the\n  2237\t    grown code space at the same absolute `:return-pc`; a\n  2238\t    continuation lifted after an attach and lowered into a fresh\n  2239\t    kernel places every pc by the receiving offset table; two\n  2240\t    waiters holding images of different lengths each lower the same\n  2241\t    slice against their own coordinates and apply the export\n  2242\t    correctly.\n  2243\t18. Under `:derivation :verifying`, a manifest whose record names a\n  2244\t    profile the linker does not implement is `:unverified-derivation`,\n  2245\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  2246\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  2247\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  2248\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  2249\t20. A closure re-exported from a transitive dependency lifts with that\n  2250\t    dependency's image as origin, the parent loads that image before\n  2251\t    lowering, and an origin the scheduler never verified is\n  2252\t    `:foreign-image`; a positional marker offered to a named kernel is\n  2253\t    `:binding-mismatch`.\n  2254\t21. An exact duplicate of a valid envelope, appended any number of\n  2255\t    times, is honored exactly once and never marks its principal as\n  2256\t    equivocating; a replayed envelope with an old sequence, an envelope\n  2257\t    at or below a principal's floor, two distinct envelopes with one\n  2258\t    sequence, a retraction naming no assertion, and a retraction by\n  2259\t    another principal are each discarded with the stated kind; a\n  2260\t    retraction bound to an assertion's id removes that assertion only.\n  2261\t22. One four-way manifest links through all four kernels with no\n  2262\t    `:contract-mismatch`; a manifest of another schema version is\n  2263\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`; a derivation without a\n  2264\t    contract entry is `:descriptor-defect` with rule\n  2265\t    `:contract-missing`.\n  2266\t23. On every backend, a module that binds `(def x 1)` and exports a\n  2267\t    closure reading `x` links, and the closure applied in the parent\n  2268\t    reads the module's `x`, while a parent binding of the same name\n  2269\t    neither supplies nor shadows it; a write the closure makes to\n  2270\t    `x` through a direct `:store-put` instruction is visible to a\n  2271\t    sibling export applied afterwards in the same task and to no\n  2272\t    other task's module store; the same module linked by two tasks\n  2273\t    holds two isolated stores; a slice whose exports reach a\n  2274\t    dependency's store transitively carries that dependency's\n  2275\t    snapshot, including a mutation the child made through the\n  2276\t    dependency's closure, a missing snapshot is\n  2277\t    `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind :missing-module-store`,\n  2278\t    and a receiving task that already holds the dependency's store\n  2279\t    keeps its own instance; a module closure calling another\n  2280\t    module's closure routes each body's reads and writes to its own\n  2281\t    module; in the child, a closure re-exported from a dependency\n  2282\t    reads that dependency's module store, not the child's ambient\n  2283\t    bindings; a module emitting `[:store-get :stream-0]` against a\n  2284\t    task with a live stream at that id reads nothing on any\n  2285\t    backend, because engine resources live in the private table no\ncommit df7cf1f4ef7c52d19ce67afc83ef1ca4ddef9225\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Oct 1 20:43:21 2026 +0700\n\n    feat(yin.repl): linker over DHT slice L5 — end-to-end publish, require and portable gate\n    \n    End to end over real UDP: process A publishes modules by signed name\n    (keygen, Ed25519 principal, manifest acknowledged at HEAD); process B\n    (JVM and Node) requires by name, waits through pending, and evaluates\n    the export on all four VMs; the plain-Clojure leg drives join,\n    load-index, names, load-module and link with every section 9 failure\n    result asserted as data; and dht_end_to_end_test.cljc runs the same\n    scenario in process over the mesh seam on JVM, Node and Dart.\n    \n    Also carries the r3 gate fixes: the :yin.module/index validator\n    short-circuits before vals on a non-map, with an 80-case totality test\n    (the report's 88-case claim is corrected by the epic confirm) and\n    regressions for the direct walk classification, staged refusal, and\n    publication refusal. build-n-test.md documents the L5 gate.\n\n docs/agents/build-n-test.md                 |  24 +-\n docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md            |  24 +-\n src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc                 |  27 +-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc                 |  14 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc                 |   8 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc             |  61 +++-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc         |  27 +-\n test/dao/space/dht_test.cljc                |  58 ++++\n test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj          | 471 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n test/yin/vm/linker/closure_test.cljc        |  47 +++\n test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc | 454 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n test/yin/vm/linker/dht_test.cljc            | 110 +++++++\n test/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc        |  41 +++\n 13 files changed, 1283 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)\ncommit 00da7c5dcb6fe90b6d035e1bc2f5d814ea990dd7\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Oct 1 23:48:58 2026 +0700\n\n    docs(design): hygiene pass and post-M5 hardening contracts for the linker-dht design\n    \n    Hygiene: ASCII and 80-column corrections across the added epic lines\n    (33 pre-existing violations preserved), 8 em-dash corruptions restored\n    as ASCII --. New section 14: the post-M5 hardening contracts — the\n    cross-host kept-cursor/aliasing proof (nine host pairs, safepoint\n    behavior, lift/lower steps) and full ownership fencing (exclusive\n    custody, authority epochs, stable operation ids, atomic admission,\n    recovery, crash/partition tests) — with the UCF amendment payload\n    enumerating :yin.k/admission and the 2^52-1 epoch/sequence bound, and\n    the five-stage sequencing plan. Authored by the architect (gpt-6.1-sol),\n    recovered byte-faithfully after a concurrent-write clobber and\n    re-applied with the design review's fixes.\n\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md b/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\nindex cc816ec2..f6741f4c 100644\n--- a/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n++