master (df7cf1f4). The working tree carries an uncommitted\n   277\trevision of that document (+378/-138, including a new post-M5\n   278\thardening section) from the parallel session; not judged here.\n   279\t\n   280\t## 5. Overall conclusion\n   281\t\n   282\tVerdict per milestone: M1 SATISFIED, M2 SATISFIED, M3 SATISFIED, M4\n   283\tSATISFIED (with the DHT design's explicit deferral of 7.4's optional\n   284\tone-response closure delivery), M5 SATISFIED. Overall: the r11\n   285\tspecification is implemented and landed on master -- its structure\n   286\tcriteria, refusal vocabulary, authority policy, install machinery and\n   287\tUCF amendments hold on the df7cf1f4 lineage on all three hosts, with\n   288\tthe linker-over-DHT epic landed as its subordinate composition. The\n   289\tresidue is small and recorded: two over-long lines in the spec itself\n   290\t(criterion 4), the linker-level remote/WebSocket transfer test retired\n   291\twith dao.jing.remote and not re-established through the linker\n   292\t(criteria 5 and 10's second clause), the stale \"nothing is\n   293\timplemented\" status line of the landed DHT design, and the deferred\n   294\tpersistent stepped linker and dependency-closure delivery.\n   336\t- `fetch`: the parameterized fetch function.\n   337\t- `stack-format`: the `:yin.debruijn.code` format record.\n   338\t- `register-format`: the `:yin.debruijn.register` format record.\n   339\t- `stack-free-names`: scans free names from stack instruction vectors.\n   340\t- `register-free-names`: scans free names from register image maps.\n   341\t- `verify-same-root-pairing`: verifies an H and R pair against source datoms.\n   342\t- Qualified refusal constructors and predicates.\n   343\t\n   344\t## 11. Completion criteria: Phase B6\n   345\t\n   346\tCross-host transfer over `dao.stream`:\n   347\t\n   348\t1. (H, R) JVM to Dart transfer over `dao.jing.content` on remote streams,\n   349\t   where the receiver initially knows only the identity (H or R) and an\n   350\t   index. Includes the Dart-side client harness for that path.\n   351\t2. (H, R) Equal normalized results under the B0 normalizer when the fetched\n   352\t   image is lifted and executed through the existing semantic VM, compared\n   353\t   to local execution.\n   354\t3. (H, R) The cross-host corpus is restricted to print-stable scalars until\n   355\t   CBOR lands; no golden test pins a Jing address.\n   356\t\n   357\tRefusals:\n   358\t\n   359\t4. (H, R) `:absent` for an identity the index cannot resolve.\n   360\t5. (H, R) `:address-mismatch` when the received value does not match the\n   361\t   address algorithm and digest, tested via:\n   362\t   a. Local storage corruption.\n   363\t   b. Corrupt client RPC response over DaoStream.\n   364\t6. (shared) A DHT peer serving mismatched content is rejected before load;\n   365\t   `make-get` filters invalid peer payloads, returning `:absent` if no peer\n   366\t   has valid data.\n   367\t7. (H, R) `:hash-mismatch` when a well-stored value at the indexed address\n   368\t   does not hash to the requested identity, including descriptor or contract\n   369\t   version disagreement.\n   370\t8. (H, R) Structural validator defect in a fetched image refused before load.\n   371\t9. (R) Live-set defect in a fetched register image refused before load.\n   372\t10. (H, R) `:unresolved-free` for a `:load-free` name the receiver cannot\n   373\t    resolve through primitives or modules.\n   374\t11. (H, R) `:shadowed-free` for a `:load-free` name shadowed by the\n   375\t    receiver's free environment or store.\n   376\t12. (R) Trusted fallback from R to H that names its trust in the outcome.\n   377\t13. (R) Verifying fallback that re-lowers named datoms, refuses a swapped\n   378\t    pairing with `:pairing-mismatch`, and accepts an authentic pairing.\n   379\t\n   380\tStructure:\n   381\t\n   382\t14. One fetch function serves both stack and register formats without\n   383\t    f